# probe.uf2 is the one binary this repository tracks. Marked explicitly so no
# line-ending heuristic can ever touch it: its SHA-256 is recorded in
# src/flash/fwCpuProbe.h and checked both at configure time
# (cmake/ProbeProvenance.cmake) and at run time before the image is written to a
# board, so a single byte changed in transit is a build failure, not a subtle
# one.
probe/probe.uf2 binary
# The application icon, copied from fwcom. Binary for the same reason: it must
# never be line-ending-normalised or diffed as text.
resources/product.ico binary
# Images: the README screenshot and the recovery bitmap. Same reason again.
assets/*.png binary
resources/*.bmp binary

# The two files whose CONTENT hashes gate that image no longer live here: the
# prober's source is wiliOGBsp's apps/cpuprobe, and this repository holds only
# the built artefact above. There is therefore nothing to pin for them here --
# they are pinned, if at all, by that repository's own .gitattributes.
#
# cmake/ProbeProvenance.cmake normalises CRLF to LF before hashing them anyway,
# precisely so that a line-ending conversion on either side cannot fail this
# build. Only probe.uf2 is hashed byte-for-byte, and only it needs the marking.
